{{/*
Keep path/fpath duplicate-free.

FPATH is exported, so a nested shell inherits the parent's fpath and then the login
files re-add their own entries on top of it (brew shellenv prepends its site-functions,
orbstack's init.zsh appends its completions). fpath therefore grew by one entry per
nesting level: 23 entries in an iTerm2 tab, 41 in a shell a few levels deep.

That matters because oh-my-zsh records "#omz fpath: $fpath" inside its compdump and
deletes the dump whenever the current fpath doesn't match. Alternating between a
top-level tab and a nested IDE terminal invalidated it every time, forcing a full
compinit plus zcompile of a ~120KB dump on most shell starts.

Deduping here (before .zprofile runs) makes fpath identical at every nesting depth, so
the dump stays valid and is reused.
*/ -}}
typeset -U path fpath

{{ if stat (joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".cargo/env") -}}
# Added by Cargo
. "$HOME/.cargo/env"
{{- end }}
